M41 step 12 -- scoring the pre-registered kill condition.

THE CONDITION, verbatim from PREREGISTRATION.md (commit f809772):
    R3 STANDS REFUTED if -- on both 109MSDCF and 119MSDCF --
        f_D <= 1.02 * f_A, i.e. the deconvolving merge buys less than 2% in FRC
        resolution over the shipped noise-gated merge,
    OR if it buys resolution only by paying noise:
        f_D > 1.02 * f_A but n_D > 1.10 * n_A.
    R3 MUST BE REOPENED if -- on both stacks --
        f_D >= 1.05 * f_A and n_D <= 1.05 * n_A.
    The band between (2%, 5%) is INDETERMINATE.

STATE OF THE TWO METRICS THE CONDITION USES
  f  (FRC 1/7 crossing) : planted-blur recovery -> NO POWER -- undefined on both detail sources (both-censored)
     a10: 9/12 of the run-of-record's detail-ROI readings are CENSORED at the ring-grid endpoint 0.4961.
     a10: repair settings (4 ring counts x 4 thresholds) that are uncensored AND separate detail from flat, on both stacks: NONE.
  n  (flat-ROI high-pass spatial sd ratio) : planted-blur recovery of the same statistic -> HAS POWER; fires on the FLAT source too (rule 9)
     and on real data arm E fires it at 144.391x / 295.487x, so it can reject.

